---
// The congestion window on a timeline: time runs down the page. Each blue band is one window of
// packets crossing from server to browser (its thickness is the packet count); each green band is
// the acknowledgements coming back. A new round can only start when the ACKs of the last one
// arrive, so each round costs one round trip, and each ACK grows the window by one packet.
// The top-right corner is left empty for the Figure's enlarge button.
---

<svg viewBox="0 0 400 430" width="100%" role="img" aria-labelledby="hw-cw-t hw-cw-d">
  <title id="hw-cw-t">The congestion window doubling each round trip</title>
  <desc id="hw-cw-d">
    A timeline with the server on the left and the browser on the right, time running downwards.
    The server sends 10 packets; they cross to the browser, and the acknowledgements cross back.
    Only when those arrive, one round trip later, does the server send the next window, now 20
    packets, and one round trip after that, 40 packets.
  </desc>

  <g font-size="19" font-weight="700" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">
    <text x="90" y="26">Server</text>
    <text x="270" y="26">Browser</text>
  </g>

  <g stroke-width="2" style="stroke: var(--viz-stroke)">
    <line x1="90" y1="38" x2="90" y2="384" />
    <line x1="270" y1="38" x2="270" y2="384" />
  </g>

  <!-- Bands: 1.6 units of thickness per packet. One-way delay: 50 units down. -->
  <g stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round">
    <polygon points="90,50 90,66 270,116 270,100" style="fill: var(--viz-flow-soft); stroke: var(--viz-flow)" />
    <polygon points="270,100 270,116 90,166 90,150" style="fill: var(--viz-ok-soft); stroke: var(--viz-ok)" />
    <polygon points="90,150 90,182 270,232 270,200" style="fill: var(--viz-flow-soft); stroke: var(--viz-flow)" />
    <polygon points="270,200 270,232 90,282 90,250" style="fill: var(--viz-ok-soft); stroke: var(--viz-ok)" />
    <polygon points="90,250 90,314 270,364 270,300" style="fill: var(--viz-flow-soft); stroke: var(--viz-flow)" />
  </g>

  <!-- One round trip per window, marked on the server's side. -->
  <g stroke-width="1.5" fill="none" style="stroke: var(--viz-muted)">
    <path d="M80 50 H74 V150 H80" />
    <path d="M80 150 H74 V250 H80" />
  </g>
  <g font-size="19" text-anchor="end" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">
    <text x="68" y="106">1 RTT</text>
    <text x="68" y="206">1 RTT</text>
  </g>

  <g font-size="19" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">
    <text x="282" y="114">10 packets</text>
    <text x="282" y="222">20 packets</text>
    <text x="282" y="338">40 packets</text>
  </g>

  <!-- Legend: colour plus a label, never colour alone. -->
  <g stroke-width="1.5">
    <rect x="40" y="402" width="20" height="16" rx="3" style="fill: var(--viz-flow-soft); stroke: var(--viz-flow)" />
    <rect x="232" y="402" width="20" height="16" rx="3" style="fill: var(--viz-ok-soft); stroke: var(--viz-ok)" />
  </g>
  <g font-size="19" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">
    <text x="68" y="416">data packets</text>
    <text x="260" y="416">ACKs</text>
  </g>
</svg>
